Feature: Insert new record into purgo_playground.config_master table

  Background:
    Given the config_master table exists in the purgo_playground schema

  Scenario: Insert new record with specified column values
    Given an existing record from purgo_playground.config_master table where config_id is 101
    When retrieving specific fields for modification
    Then update src_objt_name to "ID_Sales"
    And update src_sys to "ID_Sales"
    And update f_format to "ID_MON_Sales_"
    And update s3_landing_path to "s3a://{s3_bucket}/landing/ID/ID_Sales/"
    And update s3_archive_path to "s3a://{s3_bucket}/archive/ID/ID_Sales/"
    And update country to "ID"
    And update region to "ID"
    And update affiliate_group to "ID"
    And update affiliate to "ID"
    And update src_layer to "ID_Sales"
    And update target_src_sys to "ID_Sales"
    And update delta_stg_tables to "stg_ID_sales"
    And update source_path to "/SecureFtp/-InternalX/ID/IN/DATA/Sales/"
    And update actual_file_name to '{"ID_MON_Sales_*": "stg_ID_wholesaler"}'
    And update dag_id to "LOAD_SALES_ID"
    And insert the edited record into the purgo_playground.config_master table

  Scenario Outline: Validate new record entry with error scenarios
    Given a new record with src_objt_name "<src_objt_name>" and src_sys "<src_sys>"
    When the record is validated before insertion
    Then ensure s3_landing_path is a non-empty string
    And s3_archive_path is a non-empty string
    And source_path is approached correctly
    And "<config_id>" must be unique
    Examples:
      | src_objt_name | src_sys   | config_id |
      | ID_Sales      | ID_Sales  | 101       |
      | ID_Sales      | INVALID   | 102       |

  Scenario: Handle error conditions and logging
    Given the insertion process for a new record
    When any validation rule fails
    Then log the error message "Validation failed: non-unique config_id"
    And raise an alert "Record insertion unsuccessful due to data validation"

